prompt:
Kreative Studio pose editor, animation part (STU-PE2). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no build step. The same file runs in Node 22 (CommonJS require) and in the browser (classic <script>, no modules). Use exactly this wrapper and nothing outside it:

(function () {
  'use strict';
  const NS = typeof module === 'object' && module.exports ? null : (globalThis.KKPose = globalThis.KKPose || {});
  const need = (name, file) => (NS ? NS[name] : require(file));
  // ... the code; get other pose modules with need('vec', './vec.js') INSIDE functions (load order in the browser is free) ...
  const api = { /* exported names */ };
  if (NS) NS.<NAME> = api; else module.exports = api;
})();

Angles are degrees in every API. Coordinates are metres: +X is the figure's left, -Y its front, +Z up. Matrices are arrays of 9 numbers, row-major. Do not change the test file.

Write public/js/pose/anim.js (NAME = anim): key poses on a timeline. Get modules inside functions: V = need('vec', './vec.js') (eulerToMat, matToEuler), Q = need('quat', './quat.js') (fromMat, toMat, slerp), FK = need('fk', './fk.js') (defaultPose), IK = need('ik', './ik.js').

A pose is {version: 1, root: {pos: [x, y, z]}, joints: {name: {bend, side, twist}}} (missing fields are 0). A clip is {version: 1, fps, length (seconds), loop (boolean), keys: [{t, pose, ease, ik?}]}, keys sorted by t. key.ik, when present, maps an IK chain name (l_arm, r_arm, l_leg, r_leg) to a target [x, y, z]. Every function returns new objects and never changes its inputs (copy with JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(x))).

Export:
- EASES = ['linear', 'ease-in', 'ease-out', 'ease-in-out', 'step'].
- ease(name, u): linear u; ease-in u*u; ease-out 1-(1-u)*(1-u); ease-in-out u*u*(3-2*u); step 0. Any other name: throw new Error('unknown ease: ' + name).
- newClip(opts = {}): {version: 1, fps: opts.fps || 24, length: opts.length || 1, loop: opts.loop !== false, keys: []} (exactly these keys in this order).
- setKey(clip, t, pose, ease = 'ease-in-out'): if ease is not in EASES throw new Error('unknown ease: ' + ease). Valid times: 0 <= t < length when loop, 0 <= t <= length when not; else throw new Error('key time ' + t + ' is outside the clip'). Copy the clip; remove a key whose |key.t - t| < 1e-6; push {t, pose: copy of pose, ease}; sort keys by t; return the copy.
- removeKey(clip, t): a copy without the keys whose |key.t - t| < 1e-6.
- sample(clip, t): the pose at time t.
  * No keys: return FK.defaultPose(). One key: return a copy of its pose.
  * Find the two keys a, b and the fraction u in [0, 1]:
    loop: tt = ((t % length) + length) % length. If tt < keys[0].t or tt >= last.t: a = last, b = keys[0], span = length - last.t + keys[0].t, u = (tt >= last.t ? tt - last.t : tt + length - last.t) / span. Else a = the last key with key.t <= tt, b = the next key, u = (tt - a.t) / (b.t - a.t).
    not loop: t <= keys[0].t: return a copy of keys[0].pose; t >= last.t: return a copy of last.pose; else a, b, u as in the loop case with tt = t.
  * k = ease(a.ease, u).
  * joints: for every name in a.pose.joints or b.pose.joints: qa = Q.fromMat(V.eulerToMat(a.pose.joints[name] || {})), qb likewise from b; e = V.matToEuler(Q.toMat(Q.slerp(qa, qb, k))); joints[name] = {bend: e.bend, side: e.side, twist: e.twist}.
  * root.pos: ra = (a.pose.root && a.pose.root.pos) || [0, 0, 0.95], rb likewise; pos[i] = ra[i] + (rb[i] - ra[i]) * k.
  * result = {version: 1, root: {pos}, joints}.
  * IK: for every chain name present in both a.ik and b.ik: target = lerp of the two targets with k; r = IK.solve(result, {chain: name, target}); copy every entry of r.joints into result.joints (later chains see the earlier ones).
  * Return result.
- frameTimes(clip): n = Math.round(clip.length * clip.fps); loop: [i / fps for i in 0..n-1]; not loop: [i / fps for i in 0..n].
